{%- comment -%}
  About Card — one card in the OW Landing about carousel.

  A child of ow-about, mirroring how ow-product-card sits inside ow-products:
  the parent owns the band's chrome and the carousel scaffolding, each card is
  its own block so the merchant can add, remove and reorder them. This replaced
  a fixed `for i in (1..12)` loop over c1_… c12_ settings, which forced a
  twelve-card schema on the editor no matter how many cards were wanted and
  could not be reordered at all.

  The `presets` entry is what puts this in the theme editor's Add block picker.
  Without it the block still renders and still validates, but it can only ever
  arrive through a parent's preset tree — a merchant clicking "Add block" inside
  the About band sees nothing to choose. The picker lists presets, not blocks.

  The root element is .about-card with no wrapper around it, because
  assets/ow-landing.css styles `.about-cards-track > .about-card` and
  assets/ow-landing.js measures the first .about-card to size a scroll step.
  Do not rename it or nest it deeper.
{%- endcomment -%}

<div class="about-card" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
  <div class="about-card-img">
    {%- if block.settings.image -%}
      {{ block.settings.image | image_url: width: 800 | image_tag: alt: block.settings.alt }}
    {%- else -%}
      <img src="{{ 'ow-about-card-placeholder.jpg' | asset_url }}" alt="{{ block.settings.alt | escape }}" width="1024" height="768">
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
  {%- if block.settings.caption != blank -%}
    <div class="about-card-caption">{{ block.settings.caption }}</div>
  {%- endif -%}
</div>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "About Card",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "image_picker", "id": "image", "label": "Image", "info": "Blank falls back to the built-in placeholder." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "alt", "label": "Alt text" },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "caption", "label": "Caption", "default": "Tell one beat of the story here." }
  ],
  "presets": [{ "name": "About Card" }]
}
{% endschema %}
